From f53b157f0ab42611adf79a30700daa58f06bc678 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Cipoletti <adam@amcreativecoach.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:33:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 34/49] JavaScript: optional chaining (?.) and nullish
 coalescing (??)

Both ES2020, and in nearly every modern site's scripts: a single use
makes the whole script fail to parse in JavaScriptCore 604. A chain's
checks jump to one exit that yields undefined (true for delete); a
method call through ?.() keeps its this.
